{
  "manufacturer": "Carrier",
  "manufacturer_slug": "carrier",
  "model": "RTU Open v5",
  "model_slug": "rtu-open-v5",
  "aliases": [
    "RTU Open",
    "OPN-RTU",
    "RTU-Open",
    "11-808-697-01"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Rooftop unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Carrier packaged rooftop units and heat pumps retrofitted or factory-fitted with the RTU Open controller.",
  "summary": "RTU Open is Carrier's multi-protocol controller for packaged rooftop units and heat pumps. It speaks BACnet MS/TP or ARC156 natively and can be switched to Modbus, N2 or LonWorks. Its device instance is derived from Carrier's vendor ID (16) and the rotary address switches. Points cover setpoints, sensor values, stages, economizer/ventilation, alarms and the 'system' points a BAS can write in place of local sensors.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet ARC156"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "16101xx (xx = rotary switch address)",
  "notes": [
    "System points (system_spt, system_oat, system_rh, system_iaq, etc.) must be written at BACnet priority 16 and no more than once per minute; -999 means no network value.",
    "Some points only apply to certain unit configurations (heat pump, VFD fan, economizer, humidity options).",
    "Several display names in the source table are just 'Setpoint'; the BACnet object name tells you which one (e.g. unocc_ht_stpt).",
    "Instances use Carrier's numbering scheme (e.g. AV:1901, BV:7011), not small sequential numbers.",
    "AV:83010 is listed twice in the source (ht_spd_volt and stg_3_sat); verify on the controller which one is present.",
    "Each point also has a Modbus register in the same table; only the BACnet side is captured here."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "RTU Open v5 Integration Guide (Appendix A: Network Points List)",
    "doc_number": "11-808-697-01",
    "revision_date": "2019-11-19",
