  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the RTU Open for BACnet MS/TP with its DIP switches and rotary address, then set Occupancy Source to BAS On/Off so the BMS can command occupancy through keypad_ovrde. Write setpoints directly. Any sensor the BMS supplies (space temp, OAT, RH, CO2) goes into the system_* points at priority 16 and has to be refreshed within each point's refresh window.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "MV 1002",
        "name": "occ_source",
        "why": "Set to 3 (BAS On/Off) to allow network occupancy"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 1001",
        "name": "keypad_ovrde",
        "why": "BAS occupancy command: occupied/unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 9001",
        "name": "shutdown",
        "why": "Network shutdown command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 3001",
        "name": "occ_cl_stpt",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 3002",
        "name": "occ_ht_stpt",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 2002",
        "name": "run_status",
        "why": "Current system mode"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 2008",
        "name": "occ_status",
        "why": "Confirms occupied/unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2007",
        "name": "space_temp",
        "why": "Space temperature the unit controls to"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1008",
        "name": "sa_temp",
        "why": "Supply air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 7008",
        "name": "sfan_fail_alarm",
        "why": "Supply fan failure alarm"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy Source (occ_source, MSV:1002) defaults to Always Occupied. Set it to 3 = BAS On/Off, then write keypad_ovrde (MSV:1001): 1=Inactive, 2=Occupied, 3=Unoccupied. The shutdown point (BV:9001) stops the unit from the network.",
    "heartbeat": "No general heartbeat. Each system point has a recommended refresh time (min/max), e.g. space temperature 1 min / 5 min, OAT 5 min / 60 min. The network value is only used while it keeps being refreshed within that window; for OAT, a lost network value raises the Outdoor Air Temp Sensor alarm and the OAT lockouts stop working.",
    "remote_sensors": "Write system_spt (AV:1902), system_oat (AV:1901), system_rh (AV:1904), system_iaq (AV:1903), system_oaq (AV:1908) and oae (BV:1901, OA enthalpy) at BACnet priority 16, no more than once a minute. A network value overrides the local sensor while it is refreshed in time. Don't read the system point back to confirm a write, because the controller clears it after processing. Read the matching control point instead (space_temp, oa_temp, space_rh, iaq, oaq), at least 30 s after the write.",
    "setup": [
      "MS/TP MAC address is set on rotary switches SW1 (tens) and SW2 (ones); valid 01-99.",
      "Device instance is generated automatically as 16101xx (16 = Carrier vendor ID, xx = rotary address); it can be changed with an Equipment Touch.",
      "Baud is set on SW3 DIP 1-2 (9600/19.2k/38.4k/76.8k); 76.8k is the Carrier default; 8N1 fixed.",
      "Protocol DIP switches must be set for BACnet MS/TP and the jumper set to EIA-485; switch changes only take effect after a power cycle.",
      "Max Masters defaults to 127 and Max Info Frames to 10 (adjustable via Equipment Touch)."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "System points must be written at priority 16; writes at any other priority are ignored.",
      "Never write a system point more than once per minute (60 s).",
      "Only controllers set as MS/TP masters answer Who-Is.",
      "Some points only apply with certain options (heat pump, VFD fan, economizer, humidity sensors)."
    ]
  }
